{
  "key": "gh-1292",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "fa-tokens line must reach stdout in headless/CI runs (ledger emission invisible to the GH log)",
    "description": "fa#1241/#1243 shipped the usage ledger + fa-tokens segment-close line — but the line is emitted via _logDiagnostic (agent_cli_diag_log.dart:15), which writes ONLY to ~/.fah/logs/fa.log (by design: 'TUI/stderr stay clean'). In GH Actions legs the runner's ~/.fah dies with the runner — the dmtools-agents token reporter (gh-735/#736) greps run logs and finds ZERO fa-tokens lines (verified: 50/50 newest fa runs noUsage today).\n\nFix: in headless mode (no TUI attached — the leg invocation), emit the fa-tokens line to stdout as well (the diag-file write can stay). Guard: TUI sessions keep stdout clean; headless/CI sessions get the line where the log capture sees it.\n\nTest: headless session with a closed segment → stdout contains 'fa-tokens: {\"sessionId\":...'."
  }
}

