- Plain headless → stdout ✓ (ticket requirement)
- TUI → guarded by `!_useTui` ✓ (also, real TUI never runs runHeadless; and useTui is false when headlessPrompt != null)
- stream-json/HEP modes → `io.write` dropped by HepEventsIO → wire stays pure ✓ — **no extra flag or parameter needed!**

This is clearly the intended design: the codebase already has the "stdout-exclusivity rule" pattern. So implementation is simply:

